4.8 AUTHENTICATION ≠ AUTHORIZATION
A logged-in user is not automatically authorized to perform every action.
Explicitly distinguish:
Authentication:
"Who are you?"
Authorization:
"What are you allowed to do?"
Ownership:
"Does this resource belong to you or your permitted organization?"
Business rule:
"Is this action allowed in the current state?"

4.9 PAYMENTS MUST NEVER BE TRUSTED FROM THE FRONT END
Never grant paid access solely because:
a browser redirect occurred
a client callback says success
a UI says payment successful
a client supplied a subscription ID
Use authoritative provider verification and controlled subscription/entitlement state.

